# The lists are constants of the module, read inside the loops. The look at a loop lists only what enters from in front, so such a list is asked when the walk of the typed copy comes to the read: that it is as made, in
# front of the copy. Its own type is `Array` and says nothing of what it holds, so it was not asked for the kind of its storage: the read loaded the storage and told the kinds apart in every turn. Now what is expected of
# the list is asked, and then Link's word on what this read gives: numbers alone, or no number at all. One test in front; the storage and the length are read in front; the turn loads.
# `mixed` holds numbers and a text: a list of which that is all that is known may still be of a kind for numbers, so no kind is asked for.
# `list` and `written` are written lists of numbers that nobody changes: their test for the kind is the compare with the written data, and their length is the written number: it is not read.
# f1 = sum, f2 = sumOfWritten, f3 = sumOfFields, f4 = sumOfNumbers
# -- source: a-list-asked-in-front-of-a-typed-copy-is-asked-for-the-kind-that-link-has-seen-it-give.ts
